        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): use endsWith instead of includes for _all_ action_id matching",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`isBulkActionsBlock()` used substring `includes(\"_all_\")` to detect bulk-action rows. That heuristic is unsafe:\n\n1. **False positives**: IDs like `deploy_all_services` contain `_all_` and were incorrectly removed during confirmation updates.\n2. **No producer contract**: bare `select_all` / `deselect_all` were never namespaced and global suffix rules reserve unrelated IDs.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add a **private** Slack bulk contract in `extensions/slack/src/bulk-action-ids.ts`:\n  - producer marker: `block_id` prefix `openclaw:bulk:`\n  - closed action IDs: `openclaw:bulk:select_all`, `openclaw:bulk:deselect_all`\n  - internal producer helper: `buildOpenClawBulkActionsBlock()`\n- `interactions.block-actions.ts`: classify bulk rows **only** via `isOpenClawBulkActionsBlock()` (marker + closed IDs).\n- **Removed** unsupported bare `select_all` / `deselect_all` compatibility branch (no shipped producer evidence; it overmatched single-ID rows).\n- Add grammar, negative classifier, and whole-path handler regressions.\n\n## Upgrade contract\n\n| Producer shape | Bulk cleanup |\n|---|---|\n| `openclaw:bulk:*` block + closed action IDs | yes |\n| bare `select_all` / `deselect_all` / substring `_all_` heuristics | no |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Current head:** `b610227d`\n\n**Unit tests:**\n```\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/slack/src/bulk-action-ids.test.ts\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/slack/src/monitor/events/interactions.test.ts -t \"bulk|deploy_all_services|select_all\"\n→ 20 passed\n```\n\n**Live Slack proof (redacted, workspace channel `C0BGQ1REJ3T`):**\n\n1. **Bulk row removed when last individual control is selected** — message ts `1783746112.698819`\n2. **`deploy_all_services` preserved when another individual row remains** — message ts `1783746090.752499`\n\n**Lint:** oxfmt + oxlint on touched files — clean\n\n## Review\n\n- ClawSweeper P1/P2: removed unsupported bare-ID compatibility branch; added single-ID / duplicate-ID negative regressions; preserved unrelated custom action rows\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n\n@clawsweeper re-review\n",
